#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:130
msgid ""
"Configure the Virtual Image settings (see `Configuring Virtual Images`_ "
"above for a description of each option)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:132
msgid "Upload Image"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:134
msgid "Images can be uploaded by File or URL:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:135
msgid "*File*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:136
msgid ""
"Drag and Drop the image file, or select :guilabel:`Add File` to select "
"the image file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:137
msgid "*Url*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:138
msgid "Select the URL radio button, and enter URL of the Image."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:140
msgid ""
"The Virtual Image configuration can be saved when using a URL and the "
"import will finish in the background. When selecting or dragging and "
"dropping a file, the browser upload must complete before saving the "
"Virtual Image record or the Image will not be valid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:142
msgid "Choose the source method based on where the image is available:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:144
msgid ""
"Use **File** when the image is on your workstation. Keep the browser "
"session connected until the file upload completes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:145
msgid ""
"Use **URL** when the image is available from an HTTP or HTTPS endpoint "
"that the |morpheus| Appliance can resolve and reach. The appliance "
"retrieves the image after the record is saved, so the browser does not "
"carry the image data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:147
msgid ""
"Transfer duration depends on image size, the path between the source and "
"the appliance, available bandwidth, and the selected Storage Provider. "
"URL import can avoid a slow workstation, VPN, or browser path, but it "
"does not guarantee a faster transfer. Use only a trusted endpoint and "
"verify the image checksum against its publisher-provided value before "
"use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:149
msgid ""
"If an import appears stalled, do not create a second Virtual Image "
"immediately. Check the Virtual Image status, available capacity on the "
"selected Storage Provider, appliance reachability to a URL source, and "
"any proxy or TLS errors in the appliance logs. Retry only after "
"confirming the first transfer has failed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:151
msgid "Save Changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:153
msgid ""
"Default Storage location is ``/var/opt/morpheus/morpheus-ui/vms``. "
"Additional Storage Providers can be configured in `Infrastructure > "
"Storage`. Ensure local folders are owned by morpheus-app.morpheus-app if "
"used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:155
msgid ""
"Provisioning will fail if `Cloud init Enabled` is checked and Cloud-Init "
"is not installed on the Image."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:157
msgid ""
"Existing Image credentials are required for Linux Images that are not "
"Cloud-Init enabled and for Windows Images when Guest Customizations are "
"not used. Cloud-Init and Windows user settings need to be configured in "
":menuselection:`Administration --> Settings --> Provisioning` when using "
"Cloud-Init or Guest Customizations and new credentials are not set on the"
" Virtual Image."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:162
msgid "Multi-Disk QCOW2 Images for HVM/KVM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:164
msgid ""
"HVM/KVM supports Virtual Images containing multiple QCOW2 disks. Upload "
"every QCOW2 file and a JSON manifest named exactly ``metadata.json`` as "
"files on the same Virtual Image. The manifest maps each QCOW2 file to its"
" guest device, disk size, and order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:166
msgid ""
"Without ``metadata.json``, |morpheus| treats a QCOW2 Virtual Image as a "
"single-disk image even when multiple QCOW2 files have been uploaded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:168
msgid "The following example defines a 50 GiB boot disk and a 100 GiB data disk:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:170
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"disks\": [\n"
"    {\n"
"      \"file\": \"root.qcow2\",\n"
"      \"capacity\": 53687091200,\n"
"      \"guestDeviceName\": \"vda\",\n"
"      \"position\": 0,\n"
"      \"name\": \"root\",\n"
"      \"boot\": true\n"
"    },\n"
"    {\n"
"      \"file\": \"data.qcow2\",\n"
"      \"capacity\": 107374182400,\n"
"      \"guestDeviceName\": \"vdb\",\n"
"      \"position\": 1,\n"
"      \"name\": \"data\"\n"
"    }\n"
"  ]\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

